Z||000000||86SE||07-31-2000||03:45 PM||||My fuel pump just recently started sounding wierd or funny when it pressureizes the first 2 seconds when you turn on the key.  It sounds weak i guess....dosent sound good....<P>But so far there has been no decrease in performance, idles fine, drives fine, and starts fine......when will it go out??<P>How hard are these things to replace?<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||8
Z||000001||b lo 0||07-31-2000||04:38 PM||||I can't speak for Fieros, but a good buddy of mine just replaced the pump on his Gran Prix, and he said the hardest part was finding the right pump.  He also forgot to clip off the lines before he disconnected the pump and got soaked in gasoline, but that's because he's an idiot (j/k matt, lol  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">)<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">   <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||brianp1fiero||07-31-2000||10:53 PM||||just a thought,  have you changed the fuel filter lately??   Dropping the gas tank to get to the fuel pump is a pain.  Need access to a lift and having an extra person is a necesesity.  Also the tank being almost empty is another plus.  And dropping the front end of the tank (towards the front wheels) will keep gas from running out the back.  There are three small lines connected to the fuel rails.  One has a spring clamp, one has a single "hose" style clamp and the third has two "hose" style clamps.  Don't mix these up.  Good luck, dude....||||reg||1
Z||000003||gyro1s||08-02-2000||07:06 AM||||i found dropping the tank to be relatively painless, jack stands and a jack for the tank. plan on a couple of hours and before you need a tow.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||08-02-2000||08:30 AM||||After I replaced the engine in my 85SE v-6 4spd (it took about 2 months due to my working out of state during the week) the fuel pump started whining.  I called Ed Parks to see how long it might live and he said it could last a long time, that maybe some trash got sucked up against the screen.  It's been fine for over a year now even with the noise.||||reg||1
Z||000005||86SE||08-02-2000||03:27 PM||||I sure hope it will last a while yet.......it only has 88,348 miles on it in 14 years.<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||14
